What are Platform Supply Vessels (PSV)?
Platform Supply Vessels (PSVs) are specialized ships designed to support offshore oil and gas operations. These vessels, typically ranging from 50 to 100 meters in length, are equipped to perform various critical tasks including transportation of personnel, equipment, dry bulk supplies, and liquid cargo to offshore platforms. A defining feature of modern PSVs is their classification with Dynamic Positioning Systems, typically Class 1 or Class 2, which enable precise station-keeping in challenging marine environments. These vessels serve as the lifeline for offshore installations, ensuring continuous operations through reliable logistical support.

